# Architecture

The live page is `docs/` on GitHub Pages (`herd.ofk.horse`). `USE_FIREBASE` in `docs/config.js` is true. The page talks to Firebase Auth and Firestore in `europe-west1` (project `herd-roundup-e7f31`). There are no Cloud Functions. The plan is Spark.

Camp data is `people/{uid}`, `directory/{uid}`, and `counters/member`. Passwords stay in Firebase Auth, never in Firestore. The client computes the kamp fee (55 or 365). Save checks live in `docs/profile-write.js` and `firestore.rules`. Rules publish through `scripts/deploy-rules.mjs` and the Rules API. Do not deploy them with the Firebase CLI.

Plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Copy a block twice before adding a helper. Keep a file under about 300 lines.

## Why `apps-script/` is still here

It was the backend. The page posted to a public Apps Script web app, which wrote the people spreadsheet and sent mail. Sign-in, save, and reset no longer go there. The campers were imported into Firebase.

Leave the Apps Script project and the people spreadsheet. Archive the public web app only after another camper has signed in with their existing password. Do not delete `apps-script/` while that web app might still be deployed. Sheet columns stay append-only.

The next Apps Script job, not started, is a small background copy of the separate payment sheet when an admin signs in. Do not invent a column parser. Do not route auth or profiles back through Apps Script.
